{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>He made</b> — Many commentators said that HaShem made the moon for the fixing of HaShem's appointed times, but this is not the intent of the psalm; rather, it recounts the work of Creation. And it mentions the sun and the moon but not the stars, because these two are the rulers, and the reason to mention them in this place is that they are the cause of rains according to their motion and the gaze of the ministering angels upon them, and according to the configurations of the zodiac signs that occur in them." "<b>And the meaning of 'He made the moon for appointed times'</b> — for after it conjoins with the sun, at appointed times at the end of every month the moon renews itself, which is not so for the stars; and according to the increase of its light and its diminution, changes occur in metals, in plants, and in living creatures; and according to the inclination of the sun northward or southward, changes occur in all settled regions. Some say that HaShem alone knows the sun's setting, but this is not correct, for its setting is known by decisive proofs; rather, Scripture attributes to the moon many changes in its light and motions, while for the sun there is but one way—to shine and to set, and the time of its setting is when it grows dark, and this is what follows —"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:18.033140013Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}